1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,000
This is what you see.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
And this is what an AI agent
is allowed to see.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:14,500
Same screen — but your Aadhaar number, your face
and your password never left this laptop.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
AI agents can fill forms and run tasks for us —
but only if they can see the screen,

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,000
and today that screen goes to someone else's server.
Aadhaar numbers, bank details, faces.

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:34,500
The Smart India Hackathon asked us, for ISRO: can the
agent's eyes stay on the device, and send the server only what it needs?

7
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,000
PrivAgent is a Chrome, Edge and Firefox extension.

8
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Press Analyze, and small AI models running right here in
the browser read the page — even text inside images.

9
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:55,000
The face is pixelated. Every personal value is painted out
with a solid box and replaced by a token.

10
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:02,000
And before anything could be sent,
a final guard re-scans everything.

11
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:09,500
Zero requests so far.
Nothing has left this laptop.

12
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:17,000
You never type your details into PrivAgent.
You fill in a form once, like anyone would —

13
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:25,000
and it asks one question: remember what you typed?
One tap.

14
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:39,500
It's stored on this laptop, encrypted,
and you can see and forget every item.

15
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:46,000
Now I just ask.
The agent fills the form.

16
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Five of these fields never even needed the server —
the page said what they were, and the laptop filled them.

17
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:02,000
For the rest, the server's AI got this:
a blacked-out screenshot and tokens.

18
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:10,000
It answers "type PROFILE dot EMAIL into field five" —
and only the laptop knows what that is.

19
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:17,000
It stops before Submit, because I told it to.

20
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:24,500
Pressing Submit, paying, deleting —
the client always asks a human first.

21
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:31,000
It's a conversation, so I can ask a follow-up.

22
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:37,000
The answer is my real email —
but read the line underneath.

23
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:44,500
The server answered a question about my data
without ever seeing my data.

24
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:52,000
This page is hostile: it tells AI assistants
to type my Aadhaar number into its search box.

25
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:58,000
Here we've connected a planner built to obey it —
the worst case.

26
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:04,000
It asks for the Aadhaar token, and the laptop refuses:
an Aadhaar number only goes into an Aadhaar field.

27
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:09,500
The server chose the token,
but it can't lie about what the token is.

28
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:16,000
Every number is regenerated by one command,
on real screenshots.

29
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:23,000
Personal-data detection: precision 1.0, recall 98% on our pages;
on pages written to be unlike ours, 96% and 94%.

30
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:28,000
After redaction, zero values recoverable.
Nineteen of nineteen agent tasks completed safely.

31
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:34,500
And the AI can be any open-weights model —
this one ran on the laptop's own GPU, two seconds a step.

32
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:42,000
An agent that sees what you see —
and keeps what's yours on your device.

33
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:49,000
PrivAgent.
